    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0782" n="676" xml:id="pg676"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the British Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>:</p>
                <p>I think you will be gratified by the two extracts which I inclose from letters
                    written by British and Newfoundland officers to the agent of the American
                    Department of Commerce and Labor, who was on the Fish Commission vessel, the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grampus</hi>, during the present fishing season on the
                    Newfoundland coast. The people on both sides seem to have conducted themselves
                    with great good sense and good temper.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>





